00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:33,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:12,481
<i>If it's the right person,</i>

2
00:02:12,481 --> 00:02:17,520
<i>then his waiting will surely become
your growing courage.</i>

3
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:19,200
<i>I like you.</i>

4
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:23,840
<i>And if you feel the same way, we could...</i>

5
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:28,800
<i>I don't know why,</i>

6
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:34,600
<i>but your eyes make all my unease and hesitation
vanish in an instant.</i>

7
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:39,481
<i>Maybe because of my personality,
or because of my family,</i>

8
00:02:39,481 --> 00:02:43,240
<i>I've always run from your affection.</i>

9
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:44,761
<i>But now,</i>

10
00:02:44,761 --> 00:02:50,280
<i>should I be brave enough
to hold onto this love?</i>

11
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:58,080
[Episode 14]
[You Can Be My Boyfriend]

12
00:03:32,041 --> 00:03:34,440
She's been standing there for ages.

13
00:03:36,761 --> 00:03:40,880
She could turn into a statue,
and it still wouldn't change anything.

14
00:03:44,327 --> 00:03:46,366
Like mother, like daughter.

15
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:54,640
I knew you'd come.

16
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:56,721
Great choice of location.

17
00:03:56,721 --> 00:03:58,640
- Bustling outside, quiet in.
- Right?

18
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:02,360
My studio has this huge glass window.

19
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:05,680
That's the real soul of the place.

20
00:04:28,386 --> 00:04:30,106
What's wrong?

21
00:04:31,151 --> 00:04:32,345
Nothing.

22
00:04:32,345 --> 00:04:35,800
Xuan, I'm not feeling well. I'm leaving.

23
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:37,400
Ruan Si...

24
00:04:37,961 --> 00:04:39,200
Let's take a look around.

25
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:42,521
The garden really matches
your photography style.

26
00:04:42,521 --> 00:04:44,041
Uncle Guo, go ahead.

27
00:04:44,041 --> 00:04:46,400
- Go on in.
- Don't mind me.

28
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,560
Ms. Ruan.

29
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:57,000
Ms. Ruan? You're leaving already?

30
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,080
Sorry, I'm not feeling well.

31
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:01,161
Then go home and get some rest.

32
00:05:01,161 --> 00:05:02,641
I came to give you this.

33
00:05:02,641 --> 00:05:04,141
A gift.

34
00:05:06,641 --> 00:05:08,401
- Thanks.
- I should be the one thanking you.

35
00:05:08,401 --> 00:05:10,840
Thanks for your big red envelope.

36
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:12,925
Call me if you need a photographer.

37
00:05:12,925 --> 00:05:14,281
Sure.

38
00:05:14,281 --> 00:05:16,041
Go back to your guests. I'll get going.

39
00:05:16,041 --> 00:05:17,961
Get some good rest.

40
00:05:17,961 --> 00:05:20,120
Bye, Ms. Ruan.

41
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:48,440
Try a red one.

42
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:50,000
Try it.

43
00:05:57,739 --> 00:05:59,259
Sour?

44
00:05:59,259 --> 00:06:00,610
Yeah.

45
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:05,200
I never knew you had such a domestic side.

46
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:08,281
What other surprises are you hiding?

47
00:06:08,281 --> 00:06:12,080
Anything else is a premium feature.

48
00:06:14,713 --> 00:06:16,353
You okay?

49
00:06:20,623 --> 00:06:22,481
Here, drink some water.

50
00:06:22,481 --> 00:06:24,120
Easy.

51
00:06:42,641 --> 00:06:44,000
I'm taking you somewhere tomorrow.

52
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,281
- Where?
- Archery.

53
00:06:46,281 --> 00:06:48,240
It's Zhu Dong's birthday.

54
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,740
Not going.

55
00:06:51,601 --> 00:06:53,320
Fine, be sour then.

56
00:06:53,921 --> 00:06:55,480
I'm not eating it--

57
00:07:02,961 --> 00:07:04,641
Happy birthday!

58
00:07:04,641 --> 00:07:06,497
- Here.
- Thank you.

59
00:07:07,424 --> 00:07:09,601
Nice place.

60
00:07:09,601 --> 00:07:11,240
Want a tour?

61
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:12,241
Want me to teach you?

62
00:07:12,241 --> 00:07:14,640
- Step by step, hands-on?
- Sure.

63
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:16,600
Don't you have anything better to do?

64
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:18,200
Put the cake in the freezer.

65
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,560
All set with the equipment?

66
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:25,800
Almost. Need a hand adjusting the gear?

67
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,680
What else would you be doing?

68
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:29,401
Alright.

69
00:07:29,401 --> 00:07:31,281
Here. Put this in the fridge.

70
00:07:31,281 --> 00:07:32,481
He's always like that.

71
00:07:32,481 --> 00:07:34,040
Way too eager.

72
00:07:35,041 --> 00:07:36,440
Where's Yan An? Not here yet?

73
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:39,161
He said he was picking up You An,
so he might be a little late.

74
00:07:39,161 --> 00:07:40,760
Zheng You An's coming too?

75
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:43,081
Yeah, it was in the group chat yesterday.

76
00:07:43,081 --> 00:07:44,640
Didn't you see it?

77
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:47,000
Right, you never check that stuff.

78
00:07:47,610 --> 00:07:51,040
Help! My arms are about to break.

79
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:52,601
Don't drop it.

80
00:07:52,601 --> 00:07:56,000
- Dong, help me with this.
- Ms. Ruan.

81
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,521
- Ms. Ruan.
- Have you been spending too much time abroad?

82
00:07:58,521 --> 00:07:59,680
Now you're always late.

83
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:02,521
I brought some fresh homemade food.

84
00:08:02,521 --> 00:08:04,161
- What about you?
- Alright.

85
00:08:04,161 --> 00:08:05,800
Everyone's here. Let's get started.

86
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:07,520
Let's begin.

87
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:25,880
I have a name, you know?

88
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,560
Hold on.

89
00:08:29,521 --> 00:08:32,001
Didn't Dong already tie it for you?

90
00:08:32,001 --> 00:08:33,281
- Well...
- I'll get you all some water.

91
00:08:33,281 --> 00:08:36,720
But it's coming loose. It's falling off.

92
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:37,721
- Too loose.
- Fine.

93
00:08:37,721 --> 00:08:39,241
Come here, princess.

94
00:08:39,241 --> 00:08:41,121
Tell me if it's too tight.

95
00:08:42,241 --> 00:08:43,560
There. This should do it.

96
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:45,080
Alright, now I'm going to teach you.

97
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:47,161
- What's wrong with you?
- Stand sideways.

98
00:08:47,161 --> 00:08:49,761
Feet shoulder-width apart.

99
00:08:49,761 --> 00:08:53,160
Remember to keep your body in a straight line.

100
00:08:54,041 --> 00:08:56,761
Hold the bow with your left hand.
Grip it firmly.

101
00:08:56,761 --> 00:08:59,440
Place the arrow on the rest here.

102
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:09,000
The grip goes down here,
and the sight goes up here.

103
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,121
The white index feather should face you.

104
00:09:12,121 --> 00:09:15,281
Nock the arrow here.

105
00:09:15,281 --> 00:09:17,160
Draw back.

106
00:09:18,361 --> 00:09:19,720
A little more.

107
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:24,360
Pull it straight, right against your chin,
and release. Easy.

108
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:30,320
Your index finger goes under your jaw,
and your thumb rests against your neck.

109
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:32,280
Draw to this position.

110
00:09:35,299 --> 00:09:36,743
Let's give it a try.

111
00:09:36,743 --> 00:09:38,560
Slowly pull it back.

112
00:09:42,001 --> 00:09:47,720
This single-colored feather faces left,
and then you line it up like this.

113
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:50,680
Hold it steady.

114
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:52,560
Don't stiffen up.

115
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:54,600
Engage your core.

116
00:10:03,641 --> 00:10:05,480
Missed.

117
00:10:06,921 --> 00:10:08,001
You didn't.

118
00:10:08,001 --> 00:10:09,320
I let go too early.

119
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:11,320
Let me show you.

120
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,881
Adjust your breathing.

121
00:10:14,881 --> 00:10:16,840
Push with your left hand, pull with your right.

122
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:18,560
Engage your core.

123
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:20,521
- Core?
- Right.

124
00:10:20,521 --> 00:10:22,080
Here?

125
00:10:29,521 --> 00:10:31,440
Adjust your breathing.

126
00:10:34,761 --> 00:10:35,960
You're so good!

127
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:38,840
I believe you can make it too. Try again.

128
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,440
So good.

129
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:42,881
You shoot. I've taught you everything.

130
00:10:42,881 --> 00:10:44,440
What did you even teach? Seriously?

131
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:46,720
- Didn't I teach you?
- I...

132
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:48,680
Alright, lovebirds.

133
00:10:48,680 --> 00:10:50,401
Let's start the competition.

134
00:10:50,401 --> 00:10:52,161
We'll do five rounds.

135
00:10:52,161 --> 00:10:54,680
Each round, the highest score gets two points.

136
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,121
Tie scores get one point each.

137
00:10:56,121 --> 00:10:57,320
The lowest gets none.

138
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:59,281
Guys shoot three arrows per round.

139
00:10:59,281 --> 00:11:00,921
Girls shoot four.

140
00:11:00,921 --> 00:11:02,881
Why?

141
00:11:02,881 --> 00:11:04,161
What do you mean, why?

142
00:11:04,161 --> 00:11:05,680
Why do we get an extra arrow?

143
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,921
Aren't you new to this?

144
00:11:06,921 --> 00:11:09,041
A competition has to follow the rules.

145
00:11:09,041 --> 00:11:12,241
Otherwise, it's not satisfying even if you win.

146
00:11:12,241 --> 00:11:14,960
You're not going to win anyway, Zheng You An.

147
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:19,556
- Mind your own business.
- Let's all shoot three.

148
00:11:19,556 --> 00:11:22,041
Fine. Let's start then.

149
00:11:58,521 --> 00:12:01,160
- I'm done.
- Why are you getting so upset?

150
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:03,400
I'm here to take photos, not to compete.

151
00:12:13,641 --> 00:12:15,520
Missed.

152
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:33,161
Come on, Fu Ming Yu. That's no fun.

153
00:12:33,161 --> 00:12:36,320
That's where I wanted my last arrow to land.

154
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:37,761
Nice shot.

155
00:12:37,761 --> 00:12:41,161
Nice shot, Romeo.

156
00:12:41,161 --> 00:12:42,800
Nice shot.

157
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,761
Nice shot, Romeo, really.

158
00:12:44,761 --> 00:12:46,760
Nice shot? I think so.

159
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:50,840
- Get ready to eat.
- You sure you don't need help?

160
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:54,200
Last dish coming up!

161
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:57,440
This one's especially for you, Ms. Ruan.

162
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,680
Pork trotters.

163
00:12:58,680 --> 00:12:59,681
All done.

164
00:12:59,681 --> 00:13:01,440
What are you laughing at? It's for you.

165
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:03,040
If so, it's for me then.

166
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:07,641
Now that everything's here,
let's cut the cake and make a wish.

167
00:13:07,641 --> 00:13:10,080
- Quick.
- Let me light the candles.

168
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,520
Come on.

169
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:18,440
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

170
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:22,641
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

171
00:13:22,641 --> 00:13:26,960
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

172
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:31,640
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

173
00:13:33,032 --> 00:13:34,361
Make a wish.

174
00:13:34,361 --> 00:13:36,840
Make a wish, birthday boy.

175
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:39,641
I hope that in the days to come,

176
00:13:39,641 --> 00:13:42,720
there are many more days as happy as today.

177
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:45,281
Okay, happy birthday!

178
00:13:45,281 --> 00:13:49,080
- Happy birthday!
- Thank you.

179
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:51,361
Fifteen, twenty, fifteen!

180
00:13:51,361 --> 00:13:52,401
Drink up!

181
00:13:52,401 --> 00:13:54,320
Zheng You An, drink up!

182
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:56,921
- First round doesn't count. Again!
- Okay!

183
00:13:56,921 --> 00:13:58,761
- Fifteen, twenty, fifteen!
- Twenty!

184
00:13:58,761 --> 00:14:00,361
- Second round doesn't count!
- Yan An, drink up!

185
00:14:00,361 --> 00:14:01,440
- Yan An!
- No!

186
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:03,641
- Second round can't count!
- Ms. Ruan!

187
00:14:03,641 --> 00:14:06,361
- Thank you.
- A loss is a loss.

188
00:14:06,361 --> 00:14:08,000
For what?

189
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:11,080
I had a good time tonight.

190
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:14,080
Careful. Zheng You An, are you serious?

191
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:17,200
Who said, "a sore loser"?

192
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:19,903
- It was you, wasn't it?
- You probably had a better time than I did.

193
00:14:27,914 --> 00:14:30,200
It's getting late. I have to go to the office.

194
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,281
I'm going to leave.

195
00:14:31,281 --> 00:14:33,761
- Happy birthday.
- Thanks.

196
00:14:33,761 --> 00:14:35,680
What are you doing? Saving it for later?

197
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:38,800
Si Xian, we should leave now.

198
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,680
I need to go to the office.

199
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:41,921
- We're off.
- Bye-bye.

200
00:14:41,921 --> 00:14:43,840
- Bye-bye.
- Bye-bye.

201
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:30,873
- My skewers are cold. Heat them.
- Already got them.

202
00:15:30,873 --> 00:15:34,401
- And my chicken wings. Did you grill them?
- They're on.

203
00:15:34,401 --> 00:15:35,921
Be careful. It's raining!

204
00:15:35,921 --> 00:15:37,320
- Hurry!
- My skewers!

205
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:39,001
- Get inside! Don't!
- I...

206
00:15:39,001 --> 00:15:42,520
- I'll take these!
- Don't get caught in the rain! Hurry!

207
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:45,440
It rains!

208
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:51,680
Came out of nowhere.

209
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:36,560
[Mom]

210
00:17:40,361 --> 00:17:41,680
Hello?

211
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:45,080
<i>Ming Yu, Jin Bao is sick.</i>

212
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:47,832
Really?

213
00:17:47,832 --> 00:17:50,080
<i>Come home right away.</i>

214
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:55,040
Got it.

215
00:17:55,921 --> 00:17:58,320
I still have to stop by the office.

216
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:00,240
I'll be back later.

217
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:02,760
Okay. I'm hanging up.

218
00:18:10,121 --> 00:18:11,720
You're awake.

219
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:19,520
Just drop me off here.

220
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:29,320
[Mingchen Residences]

221
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:43,440
Are you coming up too?

222
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:45,240
I live here too.

223
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:47,280
Why can't I?

224
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:49,841
Didn't you say you had work?

225
00:18:49,841 --> 00:18:52,680
And wasn't someone at home sick...

226
00:18:56,121 --> 00:18:57,881
So you were faking it?

227
00:19:01,641 --> 00:19:02,921
So what if I was?

228
00:19:02,921 --> 00:19:06,040
You kissed me without permission.
Is that right?

229
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:12,160
But you didn't react at all.

230
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:15,801
You just kept pretending to be asleep.

231
00:19:15,801 --> 00:19:18,320
Doesn't that mean you didn't mind?

232
00:19:27,641 --> 00:19:33,320
If you don't move away now,
I might kiss you again.

233
00:20:00,401 --> 00:20:02,841
<i>Love is like that.</i>

234
00:20:02,841 --> 00:20:07,320
<i>It arrives all of a sudden,
after all you've been through.</i>

235
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:38,640
<i>So, does this make you my girlfriend now?</i>

236
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:48,000
Come on, is it up?

237
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,520
Yeah.

238
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:51,760
Okay, let go.

239
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:53,260
Careful.

240
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:57,121
Can you check if it's straight?

241
00:20:58,040 --> 00:21:00,280
Ms. Zheng? Busy?

242
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:02,801
Mom.

243
00:21:02,801 --> 00:21:05,000
You came? You didn't even tell me.

244
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:08,161
You haven't been home in days.

245
00:21:08,161 --> 00:21:11,000
Brought you your favorite cake.

246
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,280
You know me best.

247
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:15,280
How are you holding up? Exhausted?

248
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:16,601
Not bad.

249
00:21:16,601 --> 00:21:19,480
You've got this place
looking like a real studio in a few days.

250
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:20,641
My girl's got talent.

251
00:21:20,641 --> 00:21:22,361
Of course.

252
00:21:22,361 --> 00:21:27,361
I've been busy with the studio,
but I've also been playing matchmaker.

253
00:21:27,361 --> 00:21:29,960
What, you're running a dating agency now?

254
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,760
No, Mom.

255
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:33,881
Look.

256
00:21:33,881 --> 00:21:35,950
My masterpiece.

257
00:21:35,950 --> 00:21:38,280
Fu Ming Yu? Handsome.

258
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:39,921
He's not the point.

259
00:21:39,921 --> 00:21:43,320
Look in front, that half-profile.

260
00:21:44,161 --> 00:21:46,601
She's that female pilot at their airline.

261
00:21:46,601 --> 00:21:49,880
She came to my opening, remember?

262
00:21:51,921 --> 00:21:57,921
On opening day,
I handed this photo to Ms. Ruan,

263
00:21:57,921 --> 00:22:02,401
and next thing you know, they got together.

264
00:22:02,401 --> 00:22:04,720
Pretty good, right?

265
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:09,680
They got together?

266
00:22:09,680 --> 00:22:12,040
- Are you sure?
- One hundred percent.

267
00:22:12,040 --> 00:22:15,641
A few days ago, at Zhu Dong's birthday,
Fu Ming Yu brought her along.

268
00:22:15,641 --> 00:22:18,400
They were even holding hands.

269
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:20,240
I don't blame you for being surprised.

270
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:22,800
I used to drink with Ms. Ruan.

271
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:26,801
I disliked Fu Ming Yu about seven out of ten.

272
00:22:26,801 --> 00:22:30,800
But Ms. Ruan roasted him even harder
than I did.

273
00:22:30,800 --> 00:22:33,841
You don't trash someone that fiercely
unless there's history.

274
00:22:33,841 --> 00:22:37,881
And yet, one photo from me,

275
00:22:37,881 --> 00:22:40,601
and they went from enemies to lovers.

276
00:22:40,601 --> 00:22:44,361
Well, that's a lot to take in.

277
00:22:44,361 --> 00:22:48,760
But you should think about
how you're going to break this to your father.

278
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:54,200
If Fu Ming Yu's with someone else,
he's going to be the most disappointed.

279
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:56,081
Dad's a grown man.

280
00:22:56,081 --> 00:22:58,440
He'll handle it in his own way.

281
00:22:58,440 --> 00:22:59,720
Mom, get up. Enough sitting.

282
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:01,520
- Have some cake.
- I'll eat it later.

283
00:23:01,520 --> 00:23:07,520
Look, the whole point of this studio
is this large glass window.

284
00:23:08,081 --> 00:23:10,321
I've just set up the lighting.
Here, let me take some photos of you.

285
00:23:10,321 --> 00:23:11,361
- Come on.
- Okay.

286
00:23:11,361 --> 00:23:13,601
But they have to be better than last time.

287
00:23:13,601 --> 00:23:16,784
- You got it.
- This glass is really nice.

288
00:23:16,784 --> 00:23:18,784
[Hengshi Air]

289
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:25,921
This is your flight schedule for this period.

290
00:23:25,921 --> 00:23:28,720
Haven't made it into the meeting room,
and you're already fading?

291
00:23:32,921 --> 00:23:35,720
<i>Let me know when you're done.</i>

292
00:23:52,121 --> 00:23:53,561
<i>I need to talk to you.</i>

293
00:23:53,561 --> 00:23:55,584
<i>Answer the phone.</i>

294
00:23:55,584 --> 00:23:57,584
[Dong Xian]

295
00:24:01,040 --> 00:24:02,680
What's up?

296
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:06,161
<i>I heard you're together with Ming Yu now?</i>

297
00:24:06,161 --> 00:24:07,520
Zheng You An told you?

298
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:09,720
<i>Yes, You An told me today.</i>

299
00:24:09,720 --> 00:24:14,401
But I remember, last time
Ming Yu said you two were just colleagues.

300
00:24:14,401 --> 00:24:16,960
Friends at most.

301
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:18,161
<i>Right?</i>

302
00:24:18,161 --> 00:24:20,321
Anything wrong with that?

303
00:24:20,321 --> 00:24:21,881
Nothing.

304
00:24:21,881 --> 00:24:24,960
I thought we should find some time
to sit down and have a proper chat.

305
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:27,401
I can tell you more about Ming Yu.

306
00:24:27,401 --> 00:24:29,520
I know him pretty well.

307
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:31,601
<i>I've watched him grow up.</i>

308
00:24:31,601 --> 00:24:36,240
You've watched a lot of people grow up.
Except me.

309
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:39,200
<i>For one, you don't really know me.</i>

310
00:24:39,200 --> 00:24:44,200
And for another, I don't need to
learn about my own boyfriend from others.

311
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:47,561
<i>Si Xian, I think you've misunderstood me.</i>

312
00:24:47,561 --> 00:24:49,040
Si Xian--

313
00:25:08,121 --> 00:25:11,760
<i>Just then, I overheard a conversation
in the parking lot.</i>

314
00:25:16,081 --> 00:25:19,080
<i>That person seems to be my girlfriend.</i>

315
00:25:19,841 --> 00:25:21,800
<i>You recognized me just by my silhouette?</i>

316
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:23,000
<i>Wait here.</i>

317
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:25,280
<i>I'll go buy you some oranges.</i>

318
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:35,120
You finally admitted that I'm your boyfriend.

319
00:25:40,921 --> 00:25:42,800
Alright then, let's go.

320
00:25:48,280 --> 00:25:50,400
Time to take my girlfriend home.

321
00:26:07,760 --> 00:26:09,320
Let's go.

322
00:26:40,601 --> 00:26:44,280
<i>Gosh, why the elevator again?</i>

323
00:26:44,280 --> 00:26:45,760
<i>Quick, distract yourself.</i>

324
00:26:45,760 --> 00:26:48,760
<i>Find something to say. Anything.</i>

325
00:26:48,760 --> 00:26:49,881
Mr. Fu.

326
00:26:49,881 --> 00:26:51,280
Off work?

327
00:26:51,280 --> 00:26:53,120
Mr. Fu, good evening.

328
00:27:22,321 --> 00:27:24,040
Mr. Fu, bye.

329
00:27:24,040 --> 00:27:25,680
Goodbye, Mr. Fu.

330
00:27:31,310 --> 00:27:33,160
Not feeling well?

331
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:35,000
No.

332
00:27:52,200 --> 00:27:53,201
What's it then?

333
00:27:53,201 --> 00:27:54,921
Well...

334
00:27:54,921 --> 00:27:58,240
Boyfriend, I have something urgent.
I need to go.

335
00:27:58,240 --> 00:27:59,641
Don't follow me.

336
00:27:59,641 --> 00:28:01,440
Go home.

337
00:28:17,680 --> 00:28:19,200
That's killing me.

338
00:28:19,200 --> 00:28:22,520
Almost had a disaster there.

339
00:28:26,480 --> 00:28:28,321
When did you come in?

340
00:28:28,321 --> 00:28:31,000
Next time your stomach hurts, just say so.

341
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:34,280
You don't have to be so formal
with your own boyfriend.

342
00:28:42,480 --> 00:28:44,683
Legs asleep?

343
00:28:44,683 --> 00:28:48,560
Need help?

344
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:50,881
Of course.

345
00:28:50,881 --> 00:28:53,040
I've been waiting for this for a long time.

346
00:28:59,081 --> 00:29:00,881
Pretty good day.

347
00:29:00,881 --> 00:29:03,240
Isn't that Mr. Fu's car?

348
00:29:03,240 --> 00:29:04,401
Is it?

349
00:29:04,401 --> 00:29:05,641
I think it is.

350
00:29:05,641 --> 00:29:07,840
Look at the plate.

351
00:29:08,520 --> 00:29:11,240
Look! Who is that?

352
00:29:11,801 --> 00:29:13,601
Isn't that Ms. Ruan?

353
00:29:13,601 --> 00:29:14,760
So cool.

354
00:29:14,760 --> 00:29:15,921
- Morning, Jiang.
- Morning.

355
00:29:15,921 --> 00:29:18,240
How did they end up together?

356
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:19,960
Ms. Ruan.

357
00:29:36,440 --> 00:29:39,520
<i>I just saw Ruan Si Xian
get out of Mr. Fu's car.</i>

358
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:41,920
<i>He dropped her off himself.</i>

359
00:29:51,801 --> 00:29:53,681
I heard Chairman Fu's wife
came by a few days ago.

360
00:29:53,681 --> 00:29:54,841
She was with her all along.

361
00:29:54,841 --> 00:29:56,601
- Really?
- Really.

362
00:29:56,601 --> 00:29:59,440
- Chairman Fu's wife was really delighted.
- Sounds great!

363
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:01,320
Meeting time.

364
00:30:04,323 --> 00:30:08,200
Hello everyone,
I'm the purser for this flight, Jiang Zi Yue.

365
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:11,280
Pleased to be working with you all.

366
00:30:11,280 --> 00:30:12,841
Show your identity cards.

367
00:30:12,841 --> 00:30:14,280
Identity cards ready.

368
00:30:14,280 --> 00:30:16,040
Sync your watches.

369
00:30:18,601 --> 00:30:21,760
Ding Xiao Qi, tell us about this flight.

370
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:23,641
Today's route is to Shanghai.

371
00:30:23,641 --> 00:30:27,401
It's characterized by a shorter flight time,
and the passengers are mostly elite travelers.

372
00:30:27,401 --> 00:30:30,321
There's a frequent-complaint
Platinum Card passenger on this flight.

373
00:30:30,321 --> 00:30:33,641
When you pass him by, keep it quiet,
watch your words and actions,

374
00:30:33,641 --> 00:30:36,641
and accommodate all reasonable requests.

375
00:30:36,641 --> 00:30:38,040
Don't stress too much.

376
00:30:38,040 --> 00:30:40,200
If anything comes up, report to me immediately.

377
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:42,161
Understood.

378
00:30:42,161 --> 00:30:45,760
If you've got time to gossip,
maybe spend it on trimming your nails.

379
00:30:45,760 --> 00:30:47,121
Let's move.

380
00:30:47,121 --> 00:30:48,760
Let's move.

381
00:30:48,760 --> 00:30:51,121
- Go.
- Go.

382
00:30:51,121 --> 00:30:53,081
How's the simulator training going?

383
00:30:53,081 --> 00:30:55,920
Not bad, just never enough time.

384
00:31:03,641 --> 00:31:06,600
We'll do the briefing on the plane.

385
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:11,601
Getting proper rest is important for women.

386
00:31:11,601 --> 00:31:13,640
Otherwise, the face looks terrible.

387
00:31:41,720 --> 00:31:43,520
Stop it. What else is there to say?

388
00:31:43,520 --> 00:31:45,480
Mr. Chao, I'm really sorry.

389
00:31:45,480 --> 00:31:47,121
Let me explain.

390
00:31:47,121 --> 00:31:51,720
Our upgrade policy for Platinum members
has two options based on points.

391
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:52,801
- One is--
- Enough.

392
00:31:52,801 --> 00:31:55,401
I don't care how many options there are.
You still didn't get me upgraded.

393
00:31:55,401 --> 00:31:57,641
Get your supervisor.

394
00:31:57,641 --> 00:31:59,400
Ms. Yuan.

395
00:32:00,401 --> 00:32:01,402
Hello, Mr. Chao.

396
00:32:01,402 --> 00:32:04,680
I'm the purser on this flight, Jiang Zi Yue.

397
00:32:04,680 --> 00:32:06,480
- So you're Jiang Zi Yue.
- Yes.

398
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:08,000
I'll remember you.

399
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:10,200
You see this?
[Platinum Card]

400
00:32:10,200 --> 00:32:11,561
You're our Platinum member.

401
00:32:11,561 --> 00:32:15,881
I got on the plane
and told her I wanted an upgrade.

402
00:32:15,881 --> 00:32:20,361
She lumbered off,
and then lumbered back, saying no.

403
00:32:20,361 --> 00:32:22,601
So I'm asking you. Did you know about this?

404
00:32:22,601 --> 00:32:25,161
Mr. Chao, let me explain.

405
00:32:25,161 --> 00:32:28,000
Since you're a valued Platinum member,

406
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:33,240
we upgraded you
from economy to premium economy--

407
00:32:33,240 --> 00:32:34,881
Where? Where's the premium economy?

408
00:32:34,881 --> 00:32:36,401
Right where you're sitting.

409
00:32:36,401 --> 00:32:40,720
As for upgrading to business class,
we checked the system,

410
00:32:40,720 --> 00:32:43,560
and it looks like
you don't have enough points for that.

411
00:32:44,760 --> 00:32:47,440
I'm Platinum, and I don't have enough points?

412
00:32:47,440 --> 00:32:50,360
This is our airline's policy.

413
00:32:50,360 --> 00:32:54,401
So what, I'm supposed to thank you
for dragging me from the back to the front?

414
00:32:54,401 --> 00:32:55,801
That's not what I meant.

415
00:32:55,801 --> 00:32:58,121
Fine. Then let me ask you.

416
00:32:58,121 --> 00:33:02,760
Are you allowed to
bring flammable or explosive stuff on a plane?

417
00:33:02,760 --> 00:33:04,161
Of course not, Mr. Chao.

418
00:33:04,161 --> 00:33:08,520
We have strict security checks
before every flight to ensure safety.

419
00:33:08,520 --> 00:33:10,680
Then how did she get on here?

420
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:13,601
How did a propane tank end up on my flight?

421
00:33:13,601 --> 00:33:16,881
What if she blows up? What happens to me?

422
00:33:16,881 --> 00:33:18,240
She's got some fire in her.

423
00:33:18,240 --> 00:33:19,561
Go on, blow up. Let's see it!

424
00:33:19,561 --> 00:33:21,760
No. She was trying to explain.

425
00:33:21,760 --> 00:33:23,200
Mr. Chao, please don't be upset.

426
00:33:23,200 --> 00:33:26,440
About the upgrade,

427
00:33:26,440 --> 00:33:30,732
if you need one in the future,

428
00:33:30,732 --> 00:33:35,440
Platinum members
can pay with points or with cash.

429
00:33:35,440 --> 00:33:41,480
For a flight like today,
an upgrade would cost an extra 500 yuan.

430
00:33:41,480 --> 00:33:43,361
Another 500 yuan?

431
00:33:43,361 --> 00:33:45,000
Why didn't you say that earlier?

432
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:46,520
It's only 500 yuan.

433
00:33:46,520 --> 00:33:48,760
I'll pay. It's about the service.

434
00:33:48,760 --> 00:33:50,720
You think I care about 500 yuan?

435
00:33:50,720 --> 00:33:52,641
- I'm a businessman.
- Yes.

436
00:33:52,641 --> 00:33:57,520
Look at me. Jaeger-LeCoultre, Hermès.
I'm a business elite.

437
00:33:57,520 --> 00:34:00,801
One time I went to the capital of France,
Berlin.

438
00:34:00,801 --> 00:34:04,440
The moment I stepped on the plane,
the purser looked at me and asked,

439
00:34:04,440 --> 00:34:05,921
"May I help you, sir?"

440
00:34:05,921 --> 00:34:07,161
I said, "Yes."

441
00:34:07,161 --> 00:34:09,401
I'm Platinum. I want an upgrade.

442
00:34:09,401 --> 00:34:11,120
"Okay, no problem."

443
00:34:11,120 --> 00:34:13,881
She dropped to her knees. Kneeling service!

444
00:34:13,881 --> 00:34:16,281
Treated like royalty. Done in ten minutes.

445
00:34:16,281 --> 00:34:17,881
The other day, I went to Chengdu.

446
00:34:17,881 --> 00:34:22,841
I got on, and the flight attendant there
was even prettier.

447
00:34:22,841 --> 00:34:26,321
The purser and I locked eyes.

448
00:34:26,321 --> 00:34:29,520
I was about to say something,
and she stepped right up and asked,

449
00:34:29,520 --> 00:34:31,160
"Sir, would you like an upgrade?"

450
00:34:31,160 --> 00:34:32,881
Exactly! We were on the same wavelength.

451
00:34:32,881 --> 00:34:36,000
- Five minutes and I was in business class!
- Yes.

452
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:38,600
But here? You're acting like you're the boss.

453
00:34:38,600 --> 00:34:41,321
Mr. Chao, I apologize again.

454
00:34:41,321 --> 00:34:43,640
I hope you'll give us a chance
to make it right.

455
00:34:43,640 --> 00:34:46,401
We will take everything you've said seriously
and address it.

456
00:34:46,401 --> 00:34:50,321
I spend millions on Hengshi Air every year.

457
00:34:50,321 --> 00:34:51,801
I even know your manager.

458
00:34:51,801 --> 00:34:54,401
What's his name, Wang Le Kang or Wang Kang Le?

459
00:34:54,401 --> 00:34:55,681
He's nothing to me.

460
00:34:55,681 --> 00:34:57,560
Handed me his business card
and bowed like a servant.

461
00:34:57,560 --> 00:35:01,160
Other airlines have pretty flight attendants.

462
00:35:01,160 --> 00:35:05,401
Little skirts, stockings, perfume.

463
00:35:05,401 --> 00:35:08,000
You all smell like sweat,
and you even wear pants?

464
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:09,201
Like sausages.

465
00:35:09,201 --> 00:35:10,202
And you.

466
00:35:10,202 --> 00:35:16,080
You've got a black heart
and dark skin to match.

467
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:17,600
And this "Michelin Man."

468
00:35:17,600 --> 00:35:20,040
Since when does a "Michelin Man"
serve Platinum members?

469
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:24,120
You're all a bunch of clueless,
ugly, half-human rejects.

470
00:35:24,120 --> 00:35:26,921
All this talking is making me thirsty.

471
00:35:26,921 --> 00:35:28,721
Waitress, get me some water.

472
00:35:28,721 --> 00:35:29,761
Yes, Mr. Chao.

473
00:35:29,761 --> 00:35:30,841
Stop! Don't go.

474
00:35:30,841 --> 00:35:31,842
Go.

475
00:35:31,842 --> 00:35:33,560
You must go.

476
00:35:34,841 --> 00:35:36,201
What's wrong, you stupid waitress?

477
00:35:36,201 --> 00:35:38,120
Go get the water.

478
00:35:38,120 --> 00:35:39,121
Go get it! Now!

479
00:35:39,121 --> 00:35:40,841
Freaking tray-carrier. What are you doing?

480
00:35:40,841 --> 00:35:42,080
Go! Now!

481
00:35:42,080 --> 00:35:44,040
What are you shouting for?

482
00:35:44,040 --> 00:35:46,361
I've never met anyone so classless in my life!

483
00:35:46,361 --> 00:35:48,321
I've had enough of you.

484
00:35:48,321 --> 00:35:50,080
You think you deserve our service?

485
00:35:50,080 --> 00:35:51,761
If you want business class, pay for it.

486
00:35:51,761 --> 00:35:53,201
Why take it out on us?

487
00:35:53,201 --> 00:35:55,000
Think a Platinum Card makes

488
00:35:55,000 --> 00:35:57,681
the whole world revolve around you
and you boss everyone around?

489
00:35:57,681 --> 00:35:58,682
Go on, keep talking.

490
00:35:58,682 --> 00:36:00,040
- I'm recording all of this.
- Go ahead.

491
00:36:00,040 --> 00:36:01,801
- Come on, say it!
- Let it go.

492
00:36:01,801 --> 00:36:03,080
What did you call us?

493
00:36:03,080 --> 00:36:05,960
Didn't your mom ever teach you
basic manners toward women?

494
00:36:05,960 --> 00:36:07,681
You called us "freaking tray-carrier,"

495
00:36:07,681 --> 00:36:08,682
- "stupid waitress."
- That's right.

496
00:36:08,682 --> 00:36:09,761
Let me tell you,

497
00:36:09,761 --> 00:36:10,841
if anything ever goes wrong,

498
00:36:10,841 --> 00:36:12,640
you'll be begging us
to save your pathetic life!

499
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:14,160
You get on this plane
and pick apart everything,

500
00:36:14,160 --> 00:36:16,480
and we're the ones
stuck dealing with a lowlife like you.

501
00:36:16,480 --> 00:36:17,960
And you think you get to judge us?

502
00:36:17,960 --> 00:36:20,120
The more I look at you, the more annoyed I get.

503
00:36:20,120 --> 00:36:22,040
I can't even look at you anymore!

504
00:36:22,040 --> 00:36:24,560
You've got two words
written on your face: "absolute trash"!

505
00:36:24,560 --> 00:36:26,321
- Who are you calling trash?
- You!

506
00:36:26,321 --> 00:36:28,281
- Who do you think you're talking to?
- So what?

507
00:36:28,281 --> 00:36:29,361
- That's you!
- What are you doing?

508
00:36:29,361 --> 00:36:32,321
Don't touch me!

509
00:36:35,321 --> 00:36:36,401
Go ahead and complain!

510
00:36:36,401 --> 00:36:38,761
- I've been wanting to quit anyway!
- Call the police!

511
00:36:38,761 --> 00:36:39,762
Don't move!

512
00:36:39,762 --> 00:36:41,560
Get security!

513
00:36:43,241 --> 00:36:46,681
You know, you were way too reckless.

514
00:36:46,681 --> 00:36:48,241
You're really something.

515
00:36:48,241 --> 00:36:50,881
That was a grown man. You had security there.

516
00:36:50,881 --> 00:36:53,600
Why did you have to charge in
and go toe-to-toe with him?

517
00:36:55,721 --> 00:36:57,040
It hurts.

518
00:36:57,040 --> 00:37:00,440
Then maybe think twice
before charging in next time.

519
00:37:00,440 --> 00:37:01,960
Alright.

520
00:37:03,841 --> 00:37:05,160
Wait a second.

521
00:37:05,160 --> 00:37:07,440
Let me take a photo as evidence.

522
00:37:08,213 --> 00:37:09,813
Lift it a little.

523
00:37:14,201 --> 00:37:17,040
If Fu Ming Yu sees this,
he's going to lose his mind.

524
00:37:17,040 --> 00:37:18,881
Don't you dare send it.

525
00:37:18,881 --> 00:37:20,480
I don't want him to know.

526
00:37:20,480 --> 00:37:22,160
Got it.

527
00:37:23,960 --> 00:37:26,640
How's Xiao Zhen doing?

528
00:37:26,640 --> 00:37:28,080
Same as before.

529
00:37:28,080 --> 00:37:32,160
That's why they said, "Never meet someone
too stunning in your youth."

530
00:37:39,801 --> 00:37:43,960
Xuan, have you ever met
your "someone stunning"?

531
00:37:43,960 --> 00:37:46,080
Me?

532
00:37:46,080 --> 00:37:47,560
I've met plenty of people.

533
00:37:47,560 --> 00:37:49,321
Stunning?

534
00:37:50,761 --> 00:37:52,600
Not one.

535
00:37:52,600 --> 00:37:56,423
Did something happen in the past?
Did someone let you down?

536
00:37:56,423 --> 00:37:59,321
Is that why you don't trust men anymore?

537
00:37:59,321 --> 00:38:01,040
I never said I don't trust men.

538
00:38:01,040 --> 00:38:03,201
I believe there's no such man
as "the most stunning."

539
00:38:03,201 --> 00:38:05,640
There's always someone more stunning
coming along.

540
00:38:05,640 --> 00:38:07,281
Aren't you about to have exams soon?

541
00:38:07,281 --> 00:38:10,361
For the time being,
don't worry about coming in to help at the pub.

542
00:38:10,361 --> 00:38:12,640
Go home and get some rest.

543
00:38:12,640 --> 00:38:15,280
- Wait, I forgot my suitcase.
- Suitcase.

544
00:38:19,241 --> 00:38:21,040
Go on, get home. Get some rest.

545
00:38:21,040 --> 00:38:22,520
And don't be so impulsive next time.

546
00:38:22,520 --> 00:38:24,040
Take it easy.

547
00:38:49,360 --> 00:38:55,360
[F1 Examination Room]

548
00:39:23,040 --> 00:39:25,480
Ms. Ruan, good afternoon.

549
00:39:25,480 --> 00:39:27,241
Where did you get the pork ribs?

550
00:39:27,241 --> 00:39:28,281
Looks delicious.

551
00:39:28,281 --> 00:39:30,840
I'm going to grab some too.

552
00:40:07,680 --> 00:40:11,080
[My Girl]

553
00:40:26,150 --> 00:40:27,591
Ms. Ruan.

554
00:40:27,591 --> 00:40:31,000
I have something to ask you.

555
00:40:31,000 --> 00:40:32,681
Say it.

556
00:40:35,321 --> 00:40:37,422
Are you almost done eating?

557
00:40:37,422 --> 00:40:39,281
Maybe we can talk outside?

558
00:40:39,281 --> 00:40:41,761
Do you see my food?
Haven't even touched it yet.

559
00:40:41,761 --> 00:40:43,080
After I'm done.

560
00:40:43,080 --> 00:40:44,680
Okay.

561
00:40:54,560 --> 00:40:58,240
Ms. Ruan, I'll say it here.

562
00:41:00,761 --> 00:41:04,640
My mentor was complained about
by a Platinum passenger.

563
00:41:04,640 --> 00:41:08,160
You were on that flight, so you know.

564
00:41:09,055 --> 00:41:12,721
- And?
- You know what that passenger was like.

565
00:41:12,721 --> 00:41:15,281
He demanded she be fired.

566
00:41:16,801 --> 00:41:18,721
You've got one minute.

567
00:41:18,721 --> 00:41:20,480
If you don't finish, I'm going home.

568
00:41:20,480 --> 00:41:22,681
It's not even that big a deal.

569
00:41:22,681 --> 00:41:26,681
Before, when things like this happened,
the worst was a temporary suspension.

570
00:41:26,681 --> 00:41:28,241
But my mentor got fired outright.

571
00:41:28,241 --> 00:41:32,841
I feel like it might be Mr. Fu's decision,
but isn't that a bit harsh?

572
00:41:32,841 --> 00:41:36,480
I know it's a lot to put on you,
but could you talk to him,

573
00:41:36,480 --> 00:41:38,080
maybe not fire her outright?

574
00:41:38,080 --> 00:41:40,200
Cut her some slack?

575
00:41:40,200 --> 00:41:42,440
My relationship with Fu Ming…

576
00:41:44,600 --> 00:41:48,600
With Mr. Fu isn't what you imagine.

577
00:41:48,600 --> 00:41:50,721
I'm not in a position
to decide something like this.

578
00:41:50,721 --> 00:41:52,681
- But...
- Anything else?

579
00:41:55,640 --> 00:41:58,480
Sorry. I shouldn't have brought it up.

580
00:41:58,480 --> 00:42:00,840
Just forget I said anything.

581
00:42:21,201 --> 00:42:22,881
Should I get you an access card?

582
00:42:22,881 --> 00:42:24,401
Make it easier for you to come and go.

583
00:42:24,401 --> 00:42:27,361
No, thanks. That wouldn't be appropriate.

584
00:42:27,361 --> 00:42:31,880
Then you could've at least texted
or called before coming.

585
00:42:33,681 --> 00:42:38,841
Ruan Si Xian, you weren't too shy
to message me, were you?

586
00:42:38,841 --> 00:42:43,960
I didn't know how to bring it up.

587
00:42:43,960 --> 00:42:46,921
With your own boyfriend?
Just say whatever's on your mind.

588
00:42:46,921 --> 00:42:48,321
It's not personal.

589
00:42:48,321 --> 00:42:50,480
It's work.

590
00:42:50,480 --> 00:42:52,040
Work?

591
00:42:53,801 --> 00:42:57,881
Then it's even simpler.
Just be straightforward.

592
00:42:58,640 --> 00:43:02,560
It's about a flight attendant, Jiang Zi Yue.

593
00:43:02,560 --> 00:43:03,801
Do you remember her?

594
00:43:03,801 --> 00:43:07,321
Which one? We have a lot of flight attendants.

595
00:43:07,321 --> 00:43:10,480
The one who was complained about
by a Platinum passenger a few days ago.

596
00:43:11,640 --> 00:43:13,520
She got fired?

597
00:43:13,520 --> 00:43:15,201
- Yes.
- Why?

598
00:43:15,201 --> 00:43:17,281
The passenger demanded it.

599
00:43:17,281 --> 00:43:19,281
So, that's that?

600
00:43:20,480 --> 00:43:25,120
Ruan Si Xian, you didn't come here
to plead for her, did you?

601
00:43:29,160 --> 00:43:31,440
You used to be a flight attendant.

602
00:43:32,480 --> 00:43:36,681
You know exactly what happens
when a VIP passenger files a complaint.

603
00:43:36,681 --> 00:43:39,720
Are you asking me to make an exception for you?

